{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "im-cook-venting-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.83: `im-cook-venting` -- inspection and maintenance at Evap Fuel Vapor Venting, the one evaporative process an I/M program reaches in MOVES 5. THC at venting (112) for the motorcycle (11), passenger car (21), passenger truck (31), light commercial truck (32) and single-unit short-haul truck (52), every fuel MOVES adds, in Cook County, Illinois (17031), DEFAULT domain, 2020, August, weekday, every hour, road types 1 and 5, from the default database alone.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is MultidayTankVaporVentingCalculator.sql's I/M: the cold-soak insert computed twice, at cumTVVCoeffs' leakFraction and at its leakFractionIM (`tankVaporVentedIM`, TVV-5 to TVV-7, through the same clamps), the hot-soak and operating modes read at meanBaseRate and meanBaseRateIM, and the two blended per output row by IMAdjustFract (`GREATEST(quantIM x f + quant x (1 - f), 0)`, :2029-2036). Cook's 2020 venting programs cover 21, 31 and 32 at model years 1996-2016 (test standards 43; IMFactor 0.05-0.58, by age group) and 52 at 1968-2015 -- but IMFactor has no venting row for 52, so its program applies nothing, as in the SQL's inner join. Every hour, so the off-network link weights the cold soak (operating mode 151) at hours the tank warms. No row reaches the clamp (no MOVES row is 0).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the chain's `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 4 and `n_physicsRow` 29 as in `im-cook`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "inspection-maintenance"
    ]
  },
